<!--
  Corner-radius mockup CANDIDATE (not the picker screen) — a composite strip
  of button + card + input + avatar, all sharing ONE --radius value, per
  references/comparison-guidelines.md. Radius reads very differently on
  small vs. large elements, so all four must be judged together, not as an
  isolated swatch.

  Fill in {{RADIUS}} (a CSS length, e.g. "0px", "4px", "10px", "999px") and
  {{LABEL}}, delete this comment. Serve this as its own page, screenshot it,
  then reference the screenshot from templates/cards-grid.html.tmpl.

  Do NOT hardcode border-radius:50% on the avatar — it uses var(--radius)
  like everything else, so a large radius (e.g. 999px) naturally reads as a
  circle and a small radius (e.g. 0px/4px) naturally reads as a square /
  rounded-square. That's the point of the comparison: the same token applied
  consistently across very different element sizes.
-->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>
  :root { --radius: {{RADIUS}}; }
  body { margin:0; padding:2rem; font-family:-apple-system,sans-serif; background:#0e0e10; color:#eaeaea; }
  .label { font-size:0.75rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.05em; opacity:0.6; margin:0 0 1.25rem; }
  .strip { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1.5rem; flex-wrap:wrap; }

  .btn { font-family:inherit; font-weight:600; font-size:0.95rem; cursor:pointer;
         border:none; padding:0.7rem 1.4rem; border-radius: var(--radius);
         background:#3a5bd9; color:#fff; }

  .card { width:200px; border:1px solid #2a2a2e; background:#18181b;
          border-radius: var(--radius); overflow:hidden; }
  .card-header { padding:0.7rem 0.9rem; background:#222226; font-weight:600; font-size:0.85rem; }
  .card-body { padding:0.9rem; font-size:0.8rem; line-height:1.5; opacity:0.75; }

  .input { font-family:inherit; font-size:0.9rem; padding:0.6rem 0.9rem;
           border-radius: var(--radius); border:1px solid #3a3a3e;
           background:#1a1a1c; color:#eaeaea; width:180px; }

  .avatar { width:56px; height:56px; border-radius: var(--radius);
            background:#7a4de0; color:#fff; display:flex; align-items:center;
            justify-content:center; font-weight:700; font-size:1.1rem;
            flex-shrink:0; }
</style></head>
<body>
  <p class="label">{{LABEL}}</p>
  <div class="strip">
    <button class="btn">Primary action</button>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">Project card</div>
      <div class="card-body">Composite strip showing button, card, input, and avatar at the same radius.</div>
    </div>

    <input class="input" value="Text input" readonly>

    <div class="avatar">JS</div>
  </div>
</body></html>
